---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---

<PageLayout
  title="Cookies | Aspect Builds"
  description="What cookies this site sets, what only loads if you accept, and how to change your mind. No advertising or retargeting cookies, ever."
  canonical="/cookies/"
  showLeadForm={false}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Cookies', href: '/cookies/' }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--reading">
      <h1>Cookies</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This site sets no cookies and loads no third-party scripts until you choose
        to accept them. If you have not answered the banner, or you chose Reject,
        nothing on this page applies to you beyond the strictly necessary item below.
      </p>

      <h2>Strictly necessary</h2>
      <p>
        We store a single item in your browser's local storage,
        <code>kd-cookie-consent</code>, recording your answer and the date you gave it.
        It is not a tracking cookie, it is never sent to us or to anyone else, and it
        exists only so we do not ask you again on every page. Your answer stands for
        six months, after which we ask once more.
      </p>

      <h2>Only if you accept</h2>
      <p>Accepting enables two things, and nothing else:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4.</strong> Measures which pages are read and how
          people arrive, so we know which of our services people are actually looking
          for. It sets its own cookies and your IP address is anonymised. We do not use
          it for advertising and we do not share the data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Google map on our contact page.</strong> Embedding a Google map
          means Google can set cookies. Without consent the map is replaced by a button,
          and nothing is requested from Google until you press it. You can always use the
          "open directions in a new tab" link instead, which takes you to Google on your
          own terms.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        You can withdraw or change your answer at any time.
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" onclick="window.kdResetConsent && window.kdResetConsent()">
          Change my cookie choice
        </button>
      </p>
      <p>
        Clearing your browser's site data for this domain has the same effect. If you
        previously accepted, removing consent stops any further analytics collection;
        to have data already collected deleted, email us and we will action it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we never do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use advertising or retargeting cookies, we do not run a Meta Pixel or
        any similar tracker, and we do not sell or share data with third parties for
        marketing. We do not profile you or make automated decisions about you.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Separately from cookies, our hosting provider (Netlify) records standard request
        logs — IP address, timestamp, page requested — for up to 30 days for security and
        capacity planning. That happens for every visitor, is required to serve the site
        securely, and is covered by legitimate interests rather than consent. See our
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how we handle personal data generally,
        including anything you send us through the quote form.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>